In a CUDA kernel, a warp of 32 threads executes the following code. Each thread in the warp runs the same instruction stream.

```c
__global__ void kernel() {
    int idx = threadIdx.x;
    if (idx % 2 == 0) {
        // Path A: takes 10 cycles
        doWorkA();
    } else {
        // Path B: takes 10 cycles
        doWorkB();
    }
}
```
Assuming `doWorkA()` and `doWorkB()` each require exactly 10 clock cycles and there is no other work in the kernel, how many clock cycles does the warp need to complete this conditional block?

